  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Just Transitions for Water Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme aims to help transform water management by tackling key gaps and barriers to water security through a coordinated set of systemic interventions, designed to complement and ensure synergy with other programmes and always based on strong political economic analysis.

The programme goal is to strengthen governance and increase investment in sustainable water use in land-based value chains, to increase resilience and environmental benefits for people, nature and climate.  This will enable vulnerable people in 5-10 Lower Income Countries [numbers and geographies to be mapped during BC design] to access the quantity and quality of water needed to thrive, adapt to climate change and protect their environment.</narrative>
  </description>
